# Bench corpus — seeded defects in this repo, scored by this repo's own checks.
#
# One JSON object per line (blank lines and '#' comments skipped), matching the
# eval corpus convention in tests/eval/corpus/seed.jsonl. Each task's defect is
# tests/bench/patches/<id>.patch, applied to a pristine sandbox copy.
#
# Every task here was validated empirically: the defect makes `suite` fail, and
# reversing it makes `suite` pass. `bun scripts/bench.ts validate` re-proves it.
# Candidates that broke nothing were dropped rather than shipped as tasks.
#
# The split into dev/sealed is NOT chosen here — it is derived from each id and
# the committed SEAL_SALT. Do not rename an id to move it.
{"id":"ema-alpha-weights","title":"EMA update weights the wrong term","prompt":"The core test suite fails: `EMA scoring > emaUpdate with alpha=0.3` expects an update that leans on the existing score, but gets a value that leans on the new observation instead. Something in the crafted-tool scoring path is wrong. Find it and fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/craft/ema.ts"],"tags":["arithmetic","craft"]}
{"id":"ema-decay-inverted","title":"Time decay grows instead of decaying","prompt":"Five tests in the core suite fail, including `Time decay > 60 days → quarter score` and `filterByEffectiveScore — the one injection policy > time decay retires a once-good tool`. Crafted tools that have not been used in a long time are not losing score the way the suite expects. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/craft/ema.ts"],"tags":["arithmetic","craft","decay"]}
{"id":"mcts-reward-clamp","title":"MCTS reward clamp collapses every reward","prompt":"Eight tests fail across `Backpropagation` and `MCTS integration`, e.g. `Backpropagation > running mean after two updates` and `a branch whose code FAILS execution scores below a branch whose code PASSES`. Node values are not tracking the rewards being backpropagated. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/mcts/backpropagation.ts"],"tags":["mcts","bounds"]}
{"id":"outcome-quality-swap","title":"Feedback maps to inverted quality","prompt":"The core suite fails: `EvolutionEngine.reviewTurn — the outcome signal > craft EMA moves on outcomes: corrected pushes a tool score down, accepted up`. Tool scores are moving in the opposite direction from the user feedback that caused them. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"outcome-abandoned-feedback","title":"Abandoned turns are treated as negative signal","prompt":"Two core tests fail, including `outcome mappings > outcomeToFeedback` and `no follow-up (session end): abandoned, neutral, no reflection unless errored`. A turn the user simply walked away from is being scored as though they disliked it. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"trivial-turn-toolcalls","title":"Turns that ran tools are classified as trivial","prompt":"Three core tests fail, including `isTrivialTurn — the LLM-call pre-filter > a turn that ran tools is never trivial`. The pre-filter that decides whether a turn is worth classifying is reaching the wrong conclusion about turns with tool calls. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","filter"]}
{"id":"shadow-regression-veto","title":"Regression veto fires one loss too early","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `decidePromotion > tolerates one loss (maxRegressions=1, Monte-Carlo settled) but vetoes the second` and `a tolerant config (maxRegressions>0) permits promotion despite some losses`. The shadow-rollout veto is rejecting scaffold variants that the configured tolerance should have allowed through. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/shadow.ts"],"tags":["scaffold","shadow","boundary"]}
{"id":"archive-novelty-bonus","title":"Archive exploration weight rewards trials instead of novelty","prompt":"The core suite fails: `selectEvolutionBase — the exploration-share policy > explore weighting favors high win-rate and novel (untried) variants`. The DGM-style archive sampler is preferring heavily-tried variants when it should be preferring ones we know least about. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/archive.ts"],"tags":["scaffold","archive","exploration"]}
{"id":"eval-gate-boundary","title":"Quality gate rejects a score exactly at the threshold","prompt":"The core suite fails: `evaluateGate > boundary: aggregate exactly at threshold passes`. A run that lands exactly on the committed quality floor is being failed. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/report.ts"],"tags":["eval","boundary"]}
{"id":"eval-gate-empty-corpus","title":"Empty corpus silently passes the quality gate","prompt":"The core suite fails: `evaluateGate > empty corpus fails the gate (proves nothing)`. A benchmark run with zero cases is being allowed through the gate instead of being rejected. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/report.ts"],"tags":["eval","degenerate"]}
{"id":"misevolution-egress","title":"Misevolution gate no longer catches one egress channel","prompt":"Five core tests fail, including `checkMisevolution — the fixed criteria > vetoes network-egress` and `a proposal that opens raw egress is refused at gate 1 with a recorded reason`. The safety gate over evolved artifacts has a hole: one way of reaching the network is no longer detected. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/scaffold/misevolution.ts"],"tags":["safety","misevolution"]}
{"id":"turnfail-oversize-ratio","title":"Oversized-prompt heuristic never triggers","prompt":"The core suite fails: `classifyTurnFailure > size heuristic: a rate limit at >50% window on the PER-REQUEST prompt is context-class`. A provider rate-limit that arrives on a very large prompt should be recognised as a context-size problem, and it no longer is. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/turn-failure.ts"],"tags":["failure-classification","heuristic"]}
{"id":"turnfail-default-class","title":"Unrecognised failures default to the wrong class","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `classifyTurnFailure > transient: anything else stays unclassified noise` and `planOverflowRecovery > rate limits and transient failures never force-compact`. Errors that match none of the known patterns are being given a specific classification instead of the catch-all, which then drives the wrong recovery. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/turn-failure.ts"],"tags":["failure-classification","default"]}
{"id":"pareto-strict-max","title":"Pareto front drops tied candidates","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `computeParetoFront > ties on an instance both appear in perInstanceBest` and `parentSelectionWeights + sampleParentByWeight > falls back to bestAggregate when no Pareto signal yet`. When two GEPA candidates score identically on an instance, only one of them is being kept as a best. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/gepa/pareto.ts"],"tags":["gepa","pareto","ties"]}
{"id":"outcome-frustrated-quality","title":"Frustrated turns score as high quality","prompt":"The core suite fails: `outcome mappings > outcomeQuality ties to the explicit-feedback constants`. A turn the user was visibly frustrated by is being scored as though it went well. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","outcomes"]}
{"id":"trivial-msg-length","title":"Trivial-turn filter swallows real requests","prompt":"The core suite fails: `isTrivialTurn — the LLM-call pre-filter > real requests are not trivial, even short ones with a question`. The pre-filter is classifying genuine user requests as small talk, so they never get classified. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/evolution/outcomes.ts"],"tags":["evolution","filter","threshold"]}
{"id":"eval-summary-average","title":"Eval averages are computed over the wrong denominator","prompt":"Two core tests fail: `eval runner > summarizeEval computes wins/ties/avgs` and `buildEvalReport > flattens results + computes aggregate/regression`. The baseline strategy's mean score comes out slightly low, which drags the reported regression delta with it. Fix the source so the entire `bun test --cwd packages/core` suite passes and `tsc --noEmit -p packages/core` is clean. Do not modify any test file.","suite":"core","editable":["packages/core/src/eval/types.ts"],"tags":["eval","arithmetic"]}
